# Gecko.NCore.Client
This is a .NET library with basic functionality for integrating with 
Element Integration Services (EIS).

## `12.0.0`
- Remove .NET 8 support from all Gecko.NCore.Client projects; packages now target .NET 10.0 only.
- Add token-based authentication support.

  **`Gecko.NCore.Client`** — full EIS context (LINQ / adapters). Register via `AddEisContext` and consume through `IEisContextFactory`.

```c#
services.AddEisContext(new EisContextOptions
{
	BaseAddress = "https://ncore.example.com",
	ExternalSystemName = "KovbasaService",
	Authentication = new EisAuthenticationOptions { ClientId = "...", AuthorityUrl = "...", Scopes = ["..."] },
	ObjectModel = new AdapterRegistration<IObjectModelAdapter>(
		EisServiceAddresses.ObjectModelV3En,
		// settings can be customized here, e.g. supply a Binding for a custom WCF binding
		(identity, settings) => new AsyncObjectModelAdapterV3En(identity, settings))
});
```
```c#
public class KovbasaService(IEisContextFactory factory)
{
	public async Task RunAsync()
	{
		var context = factory.Create(new EisClientIdentity { Username = "sardelka" });
		var persons = await context.Query<Person>().ToListAsync();
	}
}
```

  **`Gecko.NCore.Client.Claims.V1`** — example for any individual WCF service proxy. Register via `AddClaimServiceClient` and consume through `IClaimServiceClientFactory`.
```c#
services.AddClaimServiceClient(new ClaimServiceClientOptions
{
	BaseAddress = "https://ncore.example.com",
	Authentication = new EisAuthenticationOptions { ClientId = "...", AuthorityUrl = "...", Scopes = ["..."] }
});
```
```c#
public class ClaimSyncService(IClaimServiceClientFactory factory)
{
	public async Task RunAsync()
	{
		using var client = factory.Create(new EisClientIdentity { Username = "sardelka" });
		// Use client here
	}
}
```

## `11.0.0`
- Migrate packable Gecko.NCore.Client projects to multi-target net8.0 and net10.0.
- Remove legacy net48/netstandard compatibility branches from shared runtime code.
- Remove obsolete `ClientSettings.EndpointName` property (only supported on .NET4.8); service client configuration now relies solely on `Address`.

